k","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"],["Gepuk","dish/gepuk"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/f3/Arsik_Ikan_Mas_2.jpg/500px-Arsik_Ikan_Mas_2.jpg","w":500,"h":367,"by":"Gunawan Kartapranata","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arsik_Ikan_Mas_2.jpg"}},"dish/brigadeiro":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/brigadeiro","n":"Brigadeiro","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Brazilian cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Brigadeiro is a traditional Brazilian dessert. The dessert was created by a confectioner, Heloísa Nabuco de Oliveira, to promote the presidential candidacy of Eduardo Gomes. The ingredients are condensed milk, cocoa powder, butter and chocolate sprinkles, which coat the outside to prevent any sticking.  It can be cooked in the stove or microwave to soft-ball stage caramel."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-brigadeiro"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brigadeiro"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Brazilian cuisine","cuisine/brazilian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cocoa powder","ingredient/cocoa-powder"],["Condensed milk","ingredient/condensed-milk"],["Hagelslag","ingredient/hagelslag"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Olivia's Cuisine","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"oliviascuisine.com","note":"Brazilian-born Olivia Mesquita's blog, with a large section of Brazilian classics.","url":"https://oliviascuisine.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Easy and Delish","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"easyanddelish.com","note":"Brazilian recipe collection from a Brazilian-born home cook based in the US.","url":"https://www.easyanddelish.com/easy-brazilian-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Brazilian cuisine","links":[["Arabu","dish/arabu"],["Arroz carreteiro","dish/arroz-carreteiro"],["Bauru (sandwich)","dish/bauru-sandwich"],["Beijinho","dish/beijinho"],["Beirute","dish/beirute"],["Bobó de camarão","dish/bobo-de-camarao"],["Bockwurst","dish/bockwurst"],["Bolo de fubá","dish/bolo-de-fuba"],["Canja de galinha","dish/canja-de-galinha"],["Coxinha","dish/coxinha"],["Feijoada","dish/feijoada"],["Maniçoba","dish/manicoba"],["Manuê","dish/manue"],["Marmelada de Santa Luzia","dish/marmelada-de-santa-luzia"],["Pão na chapa","dish/pao-na-chapa"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Sobá","dish/soba"],["Xis (sandwich)","dish/xis-sandwich"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a4/Brigadeiro.jpg/500px-Brigadeiro.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"User Mayra (Maych) on Flickr","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brigadeiro.jpg"}},"ingredient/pork-ribs":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/pork-ribs","n":"Pork ribs","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 6 cuisines","intro":[["Pork ribs are a cut of pork popular in Western and Asian cuisines. The rib cage of a domestic pig, meat and bones together, is cut into usable pieces, prepared by smoking, grilling, or baking – usually with a sauce, often barbecue – and then served."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-pork-ribs"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pork_ribs"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":6,"groups":[["Belarusian cuisine","cuisine/belarusian-cuisine",[["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"]]],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Cassoeula","dish/cassoeula"]]],["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine",[["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"]]],["Polish cuisine","cuisine/polish-cuisine",[["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"]]],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"]]],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine",[["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Cut of pork","ingredient/cut-of-pork"],["Pig's trotter","ingredient/pig-s-trotter"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Pork rind","ingredient/pork-rind"],["Savoy cabbage","ingredient/savoy-cabbage"],["Tomato paste","ingredient/tomato-paste"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Edible salt","ingredient/edible-salt"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Smetana","ingredient/smetana"],["Sorrel","ingredient/sorrel"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/20/Balinese_Roasted_Pork_Ribs_-_Iga_Babi_Panggang_Bali.JPG/500px-Balinese_Roasted_Pork_Ribs_-_Iga_Babi_Panggang_Bali.JPG","w":500,"h":452,"by":"Gunawan Kartapranata","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balinese_Roasted_Pork_Ribs_-_Iga_Babi_Panggang_Bali.JPG"}},"ingredient/orange-fruit":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/orange-fruit","n":"Orange (fruit)","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["The orange, also called sweet orange to distinguish it from the bitter orange (Citrus × aurantium), is the fruit of a tree in the family Rutaceae. Botanically, this is the hybrid Citrus × sinensis, between the pomelo (Citrus maxima) and the mandarin orange (Citrus reticulata). The chloroplast genome, and therefore the maternal line, is that of pomelo. Hybrids of the sweet orange form later types of mandarin and the grapefruit. The sweet orange has had its full genome sequenced."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-orange-fruit"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(fruit)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Crêpes Suzette","dish/crepes-suzette"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Crêpes Suzette","dish/crepes-suzette"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Caramel","ingredient/caramel"],["Crêpe","ingredient/crepe"],["Crêpes","ingredient/crepes"],["Curaçao liqueur","ingredient/curacao-liqueur"],["Grand Marnier","ingredient/grand-marnier"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Tangerine","ingredient/tangerine"],["Triple sec","ingredient/triple-sec"],["Zest","ingredient/zest"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/e3/Oranges_-_whole-halved-segment.jpg/500px-Oranges_-_whole-halved-segment.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Ivar Leidus","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oranges_-_whole-halved-segment.jpg"}},"dish/fugazza":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/fugazza","n":"Fugazza","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Argentine cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Fugazza (from Genoese fugassa) is a common type of Argentine pizza, originating in Buenos Aires, that consists of a thick pizza crust topped with onions and sometimes olives. A similar variant known as fugazza con queso or americana includes mozzarella cheese along with the aforementioned ingredients. It is derived from a combination of Neapolitan pizza with Italian focaccia bread, which in the Genoese Accent is known as Fugassa. The pizza originates from another style called pizza al molde."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-fugazza"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fugazza"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Argentine cuisine","cuisine/argentine-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Onions","ingredient/onions"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Familia Kitchen: Argentina","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"familiakitchen.com","note":"Argentine recipes and stories on a Latino family cooking site.","url":"https://familiakitchen.com/destination/argentina/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Argentine cuisine","links":[["Anticucho","dish/anticucho"],["Argentine pizza","dish/argentine-pizza"],["Asado","dish/asado"],["Bara brith","dish/bara-brith"],["Bondiola sandwich","dish/bondiola-sandwich"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Dulce de batata","dish/dulce-de-batata"],["Jesuita (sandwich)","dish/jesuita-sandwich"],["Jésuite","dish/jesuite"],["Matambre","dish/matambre"],["Puchero","dish/puchero"],["Rogel (cake)","dish/rogel-cake"],["Salsa golf","dish/salsa-golf"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/96/Guerrin_pizza_fugazza_queso.jpg/500px-Guerrin_pizza_fugazza_queso.jpg","w":500,"h":346,"by":"Neo139","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guerrin_pizza_fugazza_queso.jpg"}},"dish/hot-dog":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/hot-dog","n":"Hot dog","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A hot dog is a grilled, steamed, or boiled sausage served in the slit of a partially sliced bun. The term hot dog can also refer to the sausage itself. The sausage used is a wiener (Vienna sausage) or a frankfurter (Frankfurter Würstchen, also just called frank). The names of these sausages commonly refer to their assembled dish. Hot dog preparation and condiments vary worldwide. Common condiments include mustard, ketchup, relish, onions in tomato sauce, and cheese sauce. Other toppings include sauerkraut, jalapeños, chili, grated cheese, coleslaw, bacon and olives. Hot dog variants include the corn dog and pigs in a blanket."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-hot-dog"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_dog"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Hot dog bun","ingredient/hot-dog-bun"],["Vienna sausage","ingredient/vienna-sausage"]]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"],["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"],["Chow-chow (food)","dish/chow-chow-food"],["Chowder","dish/chowder"],["Cioppino","dish/cioppino"],["Clam chowder","dish/clam-chowder"],["Clam dip","dish/clam-dip"],["Club sandwich","dish/club-sandwich"],["Cobb salad","dish/cobb-salad"],["Cobbler (food)","dish/cobbler-food"],["Cook's Corner","dish/cook-s-corner"],["Crab cake","dish/crab-cake"],["Croffle","dish/croffle"],["Dagwood Bumstead","dish/dagwood-bumstead"],["Dagwood sandwich","dish/dagwood-sandwich"],["Deep-dish pizza","dish/deep-dish-pizza"],["Desperation pie","dish/desperation-pie"],["Dirty rice","dish/dirty-rice"],["Donut hole","dish/donut-hole"],["Egg in the basket","dish/egg-in-the-basket"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/fb/Hotdog_-_Evan_Swigart.jpg/500px-Hotdog_-_Evan_Swigart.jpg","w":500,"h":332,"by":"Evan Swigart from Chicago, USA","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hotdog_-_Evan_Swigart.jpg"}},"ingredient/pindang":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/pindang","n":"Pindang","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Pindang refers to a cooking method in the Indonesian and Malay language of boiling ingredients in brine or acidic solutions. Usually employed to cook fish or egg, the technique is native to Sumatra especially in Palembang, but has spread to Java and Kalimantan. The term also could refer to a specific sour and spicy fish soup which employs seasonings like tamarind. Pindang has food preservation properties, which extends the shelf life of fish products."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-pindang"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pindang"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Kapurung","dish/kapurung"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Anchovy","ingredient/anchovy"],["Asparagus bean","ingredient/asparagus-bean"],["Cayenne pepper","ingredient/cayenne-pepper"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Maize","ingredient/maize"],["Moringa (genus)","ingredient/moringa-genus"],["Sago","ingredient/sago"],["Shrimp paste","ingredient/shrimp-paste"],["Water spinach","ingredient/water-spinach"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/6b/Pindang_Patin_Palembang_2.jpg/500px-Pindang_Patin_Palembang_2.jpg","w":500,"h":343,"by":"Gunawan Kartapranata","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pindang_Patin_Palembang_2.jpg"}},"dish/kourdass":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kourdass","n":"Kourdass","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#e46a3f","intro":[["Kourdass is a Moroccan and Algerian food similar to sausage made with lamb offal that is salted, marinated, sun-dried, then boiled. It is served for special events like weddings, festivals, Moussem, and Ashura."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kourdass"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kourdass"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Algerian cuisine","cuisine/algerian-cuisine"],["Moroccan cuisine","cuisine/moroccan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Amour de Cuisine","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"amourdecuisine.fr","note":"Algerian home cooking and pastries from Algerian born cook Soulef Zaoui, in English and French.","url":"https://www.amourdecuisine.fr/en","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"My Moroccan Food","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"mymoroccanfood.com","note":"Moroccan recipe blog linked to cookbook author Nargisse Benkabbou, covering breads, soups and tagines.","url":"https://www.mymoroccanfood.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Taste of Maroc","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"tasteofmaroc.com","note":"Moroccan recipes and tutorials from Christine Benlafquih, formerly the Moroccan food writer at The Spruce Eats.","url":"https://tasteofmaroc.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"},{"name":"Salima's Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"salimaskitchen.com","note":"Moroccan section of Salima Benkhalti's blog, drawing on her family cooking.","url":"https://salimaskitchen.com/category/moroccan/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Algerian cuisine","links":[["Couscous","dish/couscous"],["Karantika","dish/karantika"],["Mbesses","dish/mbesses"],["Mhancha","dish