,"r":"dish/kak-ik","n":"Kak'ik","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A spicy red turkey soup from the Q'eqchi' ",["Maya","cuisine/maya-cuisine"]," of Alta Verapaz, Guatemala, made with tomatoes, chiles, cilantro and ",["achiote","ingredient/annatto"],". It goes back before the Spanish conquest, it's eaten at weddings and other big days, and Guatemala declared it part of its intangible heritage in 2007."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"Atlas Obscura, Kak'ik","url":"https://atlasobscura.com/foods/kakik-kaqik-guatemala-turkey-soup"},{"name":"Wanderlust, Maya food in Guatemala","url":"https://www.wanderlustmagazine.com/inspiration/maya-food-guatemala/"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kak-ik"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kak'ik"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Maya cuisine","cuisine/maya-cuisine"],["Guatemalan cuisine","cuisine/guatemalan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Achiote","ingredient/annatto"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Turkey meat","ingredient/turkey-meat"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Foodies' Kitchen: Guatemalan Recipe Collection","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thefoodieskitchen.com","note":"Index of Guatemalan recipes on a home cooking blog.","url":"https://www.thefoodieskitchen.com/2011/09/12/guatemalan-recipe-collection/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Familia Kitchen: Argentina","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"familiakitchen.com","note":"Guatemalan recipes and stories on a Latino family cooking site.","url":"https://familiakitchen.com/destination/guatemala/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Maya cuisine","links":[["Cochinita pibil","dish/cochinita-pibil"],["Pib","dish/piib"],["Tamale","dish/tamale"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/b4/2010.05.13.141849_Kac-iq_Fonda_Calle_Real_Antigua_Guatemala.jpg/500px-2010.